,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":9.769134855,"data":"    TinyGrad's float32 `/` is lowered in the Tensor API — above the scheduler, above backend selection — to `a · fl32(1/b)`, so on every backend that does not itself render a real divide it returns a value bit-identical to a correctly rounded reciprocal followed by one correctly rounded float32 multiply; the result is wrong by exactly 1 ULP in 25.9%-27.0% of general `a/b` cases — a rate that depends on the divisor law, so it travels with the pair `(a,b)` and not with the operation — and no user-facing knob changes any of this.\n"}
